<% content_for :title, "About · Nuclear Directory" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <link rel="canonical" href="<%= about_url %>">
  <meta name="description" content="Nuclear Directory is a free, sourced reference to the companies and plants of the US nuclear industry. How it is checked, how it is licensed and how to cite it.">
<% end %>
<%= render "shared/site_header" %>

<main class="nd-page nd-page--narrow nd-prose">
  <h1 class="type-title-md">About</h1>
  <p class="type-body"><strong>In short:</strong> Nuclear Directory is a free reference to the companies and plants of the US nuclear industry. Every fact comes from a public source, listed on its page.</p>

  <section aria-labelledby="what">
    <h2 id="what" class="type-body-strong">What it is</h2>
    <p class="type-body">The directory lists US companies, power plants and sites across the whole industry, from fuel and reactor developers to waste, research and investors. It also shows how they are connected: who owns, operates, supplies or buys from whom.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="checked">
    <h2 id="checked" class="type-body-strong">How it is checked</h2>
    <ul class="type-body">
      <li>A fact is published only with a public source: a regulator or agency record, a filing, the party's own announcement, or named news or trade reporting. A power deal, investment or award needs a regulator, filing or party source.</li>
      <li>Directories and aggregators are leads, never sources.</li>
      <li>Sources are listed on each page, and each page shows when it was last checked.</li>
      <li>Corrections are checked against the source before anything changes.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="type-body">See also the <%= link_to "disclaimer", disclaimer_path, class: "nd-link" %>.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="licences">
    <h2 id="licences" class="type-body-strong">Licences</h2>
    <ul class="type-body">
      <li>The code is open source under the <%= link_to "MIT License", "https://github.com/tosinoladokun/nuclear-directory/blob/main/LICENSE", class: "nd-link", rel: "noopener noreferrer" %>.</li>
      <li>The data is open under <%= link_to "CC BY 4.0", "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", class: "nd-link", rel: "noopener noreferrer" %>. Reuse it with credit.</li>
      <li>Short source quotations stay the property of their owners.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="cite">
    <h2 id="cite" class="type-body-strong">How to cite</h2>
    <p class="type-body">Cite the dataset, and say which release you used and the day you downloaded it:</p>
    <p class="type-data">Nuclear Directory (2026). <%= link_to "doi:10.5281/zenodo.23703377", "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23703377", class: "nd-link", rel: "noopener noreferrer" %></p>
    <p class="type-body">The files, the schema and the full citation are on the <%= link_to "data page", data_path, class: "nd-link" %>.</p>
    <p class="type-body">That DOI covers every release. Each release has its own version DOI on Zenodo, and its README gives the full citation.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="thanks">
    <h2 id="thanks" class="type-body-strong">Thanks</h2>
    <p class="type-body">Hosting is supported by <%= link_to "Render", "https://render.com", class: "nd-link", rel: "noopener noreferrer", target: "_blank" %>.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 id="contact" class="type-body-strong">Contact</h2>
    <p class="type-body">Found a mistake or have a source we missed? Email <%= mail_to DirectoryHelper::CORRECTIONS_EMAIL, nil, class: "nd-link" %>.</p>
  </section>
</main>
